76cc8/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fintegration-proposal%2Fparent-apply-preflight-v1.json","raw_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/raw/b8a4b13ca96709b1adff0d1907814dc3d3d76cc8/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fintegration-proposal%2Fparent-apply-preflight-v1.json","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/contents/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fintegration-proposal%2Fparent-apply-preflight-v1.json?ref=b8a4b13ca96709b1adff0d1907814dc3d3d76cc8","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@\n+{\n+  \"status\": \"dry-run exact approved append serialization; NO product writes\",\n+  \"proposal_sha256\": \"2e8cbc6a7e24f0f8fe6e7547ee26b43037a918e609b8cf617f5fc66852af4561\",\n+  \"results\": [\n+    {\n+      \"file\": \"website/content/chapters.json\",\n+      \"approved_after_sha256\": \"17fe0e096447259511e706179a8ebe5eae4d19a6b26764ccd073d02e287db795\",\n+      \"ensure_ascii\": false,\n+      \"append_count\": 1\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"file\": \"website/content/readings.json\",\n+      \"approved_after_sha256\": \"fa35944998387cf579ca9b88c71bcf1d73e2b0400335c17cb6938d54a8fa26f2\",\n+      \"ensure_ascii\": false,\n+      \"append_count\": 1\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"file\": \"website/content/highlights.json\",\n+      \"approved_after_sha256\": \"671cc9950ce54efeca34a768003d3a20fcdb89915050964d1a5f4ef72cc60916\",\n+      \"ensure_ascii\": false,\n+      \"append_count\": 3\n+    }\n+  ]\n+}"},{"sha":"e0e175d98c86cc0e498905a4d6c6b8523589c679","filename":"runs/online-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011/integration-proposal/plan-v1.md","status":"added","additions":13,"deletions":0,"changes":13,"blob_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/blob/b8a4b13ca96709b1adff0d1907814dc3d3d76cc8/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fintegration-proposal%2Fplan-v1.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/raw/b8a4b13ca96709b1adff0d1907814dc3d3d76cc8/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fintegration-proposal%2Fplan-v1.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/contents/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fintegration-proposal%2Fplan-v1.md?ref=b8a4b13ca96709b1adff0d1907814dc3d3d76cc8","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@\n+# Prescient Euclidean Book integration proposal\n+\n+One source-card group and one coherent lesson represented by three adjacent declaration-bound highlights: geometry, variable bound, fixed bound. The existing schema has one full_name per highlight; no fabricated grouping field or synthetic Book node is introduced. One production root import and one eventual Test import are proposed, plus one online-ogd module glob. The Test import remains conditional on exact accepted file binding.\n+\n+All21 old source cards and other parsed objects survive the in-memory append/reverse audit; historical completion blobs are untouched. Proposed source-card total22 is an implementation count, not a source denominator. Three canonical new declaration nodes must be bound to real compiled declarations and checked against every old registry object after authorized build.\n+\n+The payload supplies exact geometry and both signed half-square bounds, actual-run equality, current-loss-before-output/new-state scoring, arbitrary genuine EReal loss conditions, hmin valid-run scope, initial point outsideV allowed, variable previous-state max/lasteta and fixedT0. Explicit atomic binder/conclusion audit is in JSON. Raw module headers have ambient section parameters: validate their raw text separately from complete compiled TYPE and preserve complete ambient assumptions in reader prose.\n+\n+Author optimality/global-support justification remains an unresolved source gap in the approved source topology. A successful alternative implementation would not certify that author step. Fixed-step proof-left-as-exercise remains mandatory. Source topology, actual Lean VALUE occurrences, compressed teaching lesson and conceptual Functor transport are separate layers. Selected actual VALUE references were read from the export, not inferred from imports; no necessity or complete graph claim. No candidate BODY was read.\n+\n+Before any apply, independent review must bind the source module receipt, current TYPE/VALUE export, topologyV2 and its review, exact roots/metadata before hashes and eventually Test ownership. After approved append, run shared library/Tests/full harness, diff-aware contributor check, generated Book registry preservation, source-card and formula checks, folded exact headers/full-proof source links, and visual geometry review. Pin source links only once the exact accepted source commit is known; no invented commit URL. Do not read proposed imports as already applied.\n+\n+BODY, canary and full-package gates remain PENDING in this proposal. All7forward containers and6future claims remain OPEN; Chapter2partial, GoalACTIVE, no main/live or source-container closure. No roadmap/results milestone, coverage, old manifests, compressed-spine generator or Functor metadata edit is proposed. Parent review precedes product application."},{"sha":"9536d17477ed2ec9dfba6f0c0533c0998a78a3bb","filename":"runs/online-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011/integration-proposal/plan-v2.md","status":"added","additions":9,"deletions":0,"changes":9,"blob_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/blob/b8a4b13ca96709b1adff0d1907814dc3d3d76cc8/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fintegration-proposal%2Fplan-v2.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/raw/b8a4b13ca96709b1adff0d1907814dc3d3d76cc8/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fintegration-proposal%2Fplan-v2.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/contents/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fintegration-proposal%2Fplan-v2.md?ref=b8a4b13ca96709b1adff0d1907814dc3d3d76cc8","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@\n+# Prescient Euclidean integration proposal v2\n+\n+V1 preserved. Product values now use stable compiled-local wording, with package validation/source reconciliation recorded separately. No canary/full-gate acceptance is claimed. Production BODY review is bound at SHA 8b3cc4fea0b8a6988908cc7370ab67907815f1d04637f75f01241c19e052d8f4. Seven containers and six future claims stay open in proposal governance, not repeated in each highlight.\n+\n+Geometry proof prose now covers only the actual derivative and norm expansion; endpoint prose separately covers objective equality, unique minimizer identification, canonical Option-run induction and the corresponding regret bound for every parameter u with hu. No artificial geometry-only run conclusion remains. Source-gap and mathematical scope text stays adjacent.\n+\n+Atomic audit has one entry per frozen binder (including each individual V hypothesis and each ambient typeclass), classified SOURCE/STANDING/TYPING. The single frozen hmin conjunction binder additionally has two explicit conjunct audit entries. This classification adds no new mathematical premise.\n+\n+All three metadata prehashes rechecked and reverse-append preservation passed in memory. Existing21 source cards and historical completion prose remain untouched. Source topologyV2 and its approval plus actual TYPE/VALUE pins are retained. No product apply, new proof read, build, closure or status mutation. Distinct integration review follows."},{"sha":"064d33fa395a12fceec0c3b95f7420001b753c53","filename":"runs/online-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011/integration-proposal/proposal-v1.json","status":"added","additions":305,"deletions":0,"changes":305,"blob_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/blob/b8a4b13ca96709b1adff0d1907814dc3d3d76cc8/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fintegration-proposal%2Fproposal-v1.json","raw_url":"https://github.com/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/raw/b8a4b13ca96709b1adff0d1907814dc3d3d76cc8/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fintegration-proposal%2Fproposal-v1.json","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DakeBU/Auto-Bandit-RL-Proof-In-Sleep/contents/runs%2Fonline-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011%2Fintegration-proposal%2Fproposal-v1.json?ref=b8a4b13ca96709b1adff0d1907814dc3d3d76cc8","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,305 @@\n+{\n+  \"status\": \"proof-free integration PROPOSAL; independent review required\",\n+  \"actor\": \"/root/adaptive_decoder\",\n+  \"requested_model\": \"GPT-6 Astra\",\n+  \"requested_effort\": \"medium\",\n+  \"runtime_attestation\": false,\n+  \"input_raw_sha256\": {\n+    \"website/content/chapters.json\": \"74792b4767d6669e867c9034fc8eb09949360f1a1aaadcdd048ef92cb64eca81\",\n+    \"website/content/readings.json\": \"cd71475748324e9cab13ff3c0c08cd980a099e7c6ad77431185a367d2fcedde8\",\n+    \"website/content/highlights.json\": \"1c8c3697a21f24c416848938aaf54fdf9cc5566b9277a65fcaa70783bf4c7a5f\",\n+    \"BanditRLProof.lean\": \"5a0e513af1c02d8055f5ce27dab228586e7dc5c18fce7881d128b6506200fab3\",\n+    \"Tests.lean\": \"8fa5deac4df63a571c65c5180144fdad04258e7ebf852c9a87968dbc28c79a89\",\n+    \"docs/contracts/online-ch2-prescient-euclidean-v1/neutral-frozen-headers-v1.txt\": \"1d6cda54b46476323dccaeae6fc3b33e8d1494bb655b99045ea2cde569b8e20a\",\n+    \"docs/contracts/online-ch2-prescient-euclidean-v1/neutral-frozen-imported-definitions-v1.txt\": \"dff55f4b3262afa2869e8dce05cf27bde92b8ef94945f31c7a198a0c8f39c9a1\",\n+    \"runs/online-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011/source-topology-proposal-v2/topology.json\": \"f317dce023cae552746ad8ef38163e646d3b77712feffc73468ceac41efee448\",\n+    \"runs/online-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011/fresh-source-topology-review-v2.json\": \"c97719bbe8264c8d953b311d78355a1ee2d337381a5eb7c3ba1859cf26bb9fe0\",\n+    \"runs/online-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011/formalizer-core-v1/type-value-constants-v1.json\": \"32855356493f3e7048ba9eccce9d8186f2dbf48b601061f200ff5c2722929f4c\",\n+    \"runs/online-ch2-prescient-euclidean-20261011/formalizer-core-v1/compiled-candidate-summary-v1.json\": \"f2d0af705dd30a75bcd06a2c67a753a6a4c0164ab88b9256c7ad52001c2813b9\",\n+    \"website/scripts/build_site.py\": \"4fe18b8b9a543ff5256a278f49d160424b30ba2185c946f3d6081ad5460ccaff\",\n+    \"website/scripts/book_registry.py\": \"2557e84c4a60bbd659d1067843cedbe329a4c0c922244614299ae93d347dce03\"\n+  },\n+  \"core_binding_from_compiled_receipt\": {\n+    \"path\": \"BanditRLProof/OnlinePrescientEuclidean.lean\",\n+    \"raw_sha256\": \"9b755a12d540c1039b068e4b97af90ac483a58fd1a8b40af9c806264f95d42b8\",\n+    \"public_declarations\": [\n+      \"BanditRL.OnlineBregman.quadratic_geometry\",\n+      \"BanditRL.OnlinePrescientBregman.euclidean_variable_regret\",\n+      \"BanditRL.OnlinePrescientBregman.euclidean_fixed_regret\"\n+    ],\n+    \"new_public_helpers\": 0\n+  },\n+  \"core_BODY_read\": false,\n+  \"selected_actual_VALUE_parents\": {\n+    \"BanditRL.OnlineBregman.quadratic_geometry\": [\n+      \"hasStrictFDerivAt_norm_sq\",\n+      \"HasGradientAt.fderiv_apply\",\n+      \"norm_sub_sq_real\"\n+    ],\n+    \"BanditRL.OnlinePrescientBregman.euclidean_variable_regret\": [\n+      \"BanditRL.OnlineBregman.quadratic_geometry\",\n+      \"BanditRL.OnlineConvex.sourceProper_of_domain\",\n+      \"BanditRL.OnlinePrescientBregman.iterate_eq_of_source_updates\",\n+      \"BanditRL.OnlinePrescientBregman.source_variable_regret\"\n+    ],\n+    \"BanditRL.OnlinePrescientBregman.euclidean_fixed_regret\": [\n+      \"BanditRL.OnlineBregman.quadratic_geometry\",\n+      \"BanditRL.OnlineConvex.sourceProper_of_domain\",\n+      \"BanditRL.OnlinePrescientBregman.iterate_eq_of_source_updates\",\n+      \"BanditRL.OnlinePrescientBregman.source_fixed_regret\"\n+    ]\n+  },\n+  \"json_patches\": [\n+    {\n+      \"file\": \"website/content/chapters.json\",\n+      \"operations\": [\n+        {\n+          \"op\": \"add\",\n+          \"path\": \"/chapters/10/module_globs/-\",\n+          \"value\": \"BanditRLProof/OnlinePrescientEuclidean.lean\"\n+        }\n+      ]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"file\": \"website/content/readings.json\",\n+      \"operations\": [\n+        {\n+          \"op\": \"add\",\n+          \"path\": \"/readings/10/source_theorems/-\",\n+          \"value\": {\n+            \"label\": \"Prescient Euclidean updates: quadratic geometry and both Theorem15.30 bounds\",\n+            \"pages\": \"printed14,265–266 / PDF26,277–278\",\n+            \"pdf_page\": 277,\n+            \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1912.13213v10#page=277\",\n+            \"math\": \"\\\\begin{gathered}\\\\psi(z)=\\\\frac12\\\\|z\\\\|^2,\\\\qquad\\\\nabla\\\\psi(y)=y,\\\\qquad B_\\\\psi(x;y)=\\\\frac12\\\\|x-y\\\\|^2.\\\\\\\\R_T(u)\\\\le\\\\frac{\\\\max_{0\\\\le s<T}\\\\frac12\\\\|u-x_s\\\\|^2}{\\\\eta_{T-1}}-\\\\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\\\\frac{\\\\|x_{t+1}-x_t\\\\|^2}{2\\\\eta_t}.\\\\\\\\R_T(u)\\\\le\\\\frac{\\\\|u-x_0\\\\|^2}{2\\\\eta}-\\\\frac1{2\\\\eta}\\\\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\\\\|x_{t+1}-x_t\\\\|^2.\\\\end{gathered}\",\n+            \"plain\": \"Knowing the current loss before output removes the positive gradient-energy term and retains negative squared movement. The initial comparator potential can still make the total bound positive. Finite-dimensional real inner-product E with NormedAddCommGroup E, InnerProductSpace ℝ E and FiniteDimensional ℝ E. V is closed, nonempty and convex. Played EReal losses have no bottom anywhere, are finite on V, and have ambient global supports at every point of V. Each supplied x(t+1) actually attains the squared-distance-penalized minimum on V; initialization x(0)=x0 is fixed. x0 need not belong to V. There is no affine, smooth-loss, globally finite-loss, bounded-gradient or bounded-domain restriction.\",\n+            \"fallback\": \"Quadratic Bregman divergence is half squared distance. Variable steps use the maximum previous-state potential divided by the last used step; fixed steps use initial potential. Both subtract exact half-weighted squared movements.\",\n+            \"relationship\": \"Chapter2 PDF26 points to Algorithm15.8 and Theorem15.30 on PDF277–278. Both branches are mandatory, including the fixed proof left as an exercise on PDF278. Specialize X=univ and psi=norm²/2; interior, derivative, strict-convexity and closedness facts are derived rather than added as user premises. The author’s constrained optimality/global-support step on PDF277 retains an unresolved source-proof justification. The alternative proximal-comparison route does not certify or erase that claim. Locally compiled candidate; independent production BODY, complete canary BODY, combined project and final package acceptance pending. All seven Chapter2 forward containers and six future claims remain open; Chapter2 partial, accepted=false, proof denominator=null and Chapters1–16 GoalACTIVE. No source-container closure, main or live-publication claim.\",\n+            \"contract\": {\n+              \"model\": \"Receive the entire current loss before choosing the new point and pay that loss at the new point. Lean loss t and eta t are source round t+1: center x(t), output/paid point x(t+1). This differs from ordinary OGD, which scores loss t at x(t). The conclusion identifies the SAME partial Option iterate at every prefix; it is conditional on attained updates and does not assert universal existence.\",\n+              \"assumptions\": \"Finite-dimensional real inner-product E with NormedAddCommGroup E, InnerProductSpace ℝ E and FiniteDimensional ℝ E. V is closed, nonempty and convex. Played EReal losses have no bottom anywhere, are finite on V, and have ambient global supports at every point of V. Each supplied x(t+1) actually attains the squared-distance-penalized minimum on V; initialization x(0)=x0 is fixed. x0 need not belong to V. There is no affine, smooth-loss, globally finite-loss, bounded-gradient or bounded-domain restriction.\",\n+              \"parameters\": \"Variable: T>0, every used step positive, adjacent played steps nonincreasing, max indices0..T-1, last eta(T-1). Fixed: eta>0 and any T including0.\",\n+              \"regret\": \"R_T(u)=sum_{t<T}((loss t (x(t+1))).toReal-(loss t u).toReal), for every u in V; scoring is finite on V.\",\n+              \"guarantee\": \"Each endpoint concludes canonical Option-run equality AND its full signed bound. The shared geometry theorem computes the actual derivative and exact ordered divergence; on complete real Hilbert space it is an explicit generalization of source Euclidean geometry.\"\n+            },\n+            \"local_status\": {\n+              \"status\": \"compiled\",\n+              \"label\": \"Prescient Euclidean candidate; package acceptance pending\",\n+              \"boundary\": \"Locally compiled candidate; independent production BODY, complete canary BODY, combined project and final package acceptance pending. All seven Chapter2 forward containers and six future claims remain open; Chapter2 partial, accepted=false, proof denominator=null and Chapters1–16 GoalACTIVE. No source-container closure, main or live-publication claim.\"\n+            }\n+          }\n+        }\n+      ]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"file\": \"website/content/highlights.json\",\n+      \"operations\": [\n+        {\n+          \"op\": \"add\",\n+          \"path\": \"/highlights/-\",\n+          \"value\": {\n+            \"full_name\": \"BanditRL.OnlineBregman.quadratic_geometry\",\n+            \"title\": \"Prescient Euclidean geometry: the quadratic derivative and divergence\",\n+            \"chapter\": \"online-ogd\",\n+            \"featured\": false,\n+            \"teaching_order\": 330,\n+            \"source_match\": \"closest-source\",\n+            \"plain\": \"Complete real Hilbert E: NormedAddCommGroup E, InnerProductSpace ℝ E, CompleteSpace E; arbitrary x,y. Actual gradient y and exact divergence identity form one conjunction.\",\n+            \"math\": \"\\\\psi(z)=\\\\frac12\\\\|z\\\\|^2,\\\\qquad\\\\nabla\\\\psi(y)=y,\\\\qquad B_\\\\psi(x;y)=\\\\frac12\\\\|x-y\\\\|^2.\",\n+            \"intuition\": \"Current-loss access changes the paid point. Movement contributes negatively, while the comparator potential remains.\",\n+            \"why\": \"One of three declaration-bound parts of the same prescient Euclidean lesson.\",\n+            \"position\": \"Algorithm15.8/Theorem15.30, PDF277–278; C2 pointer PDF26. Quadratic X=univ specialization; fixed proof exercise remains mandatory. The author’s constrained optimality/global-support step on PDF277 retains an unresolved source-proof justification. The alternative proximal-comparison route does not certify or erase that claim.\",\n+            \"proof_idea\": \"The quadratic derivative gives half squared distance as the shared divergence. Rewrite each actual penalized objective; strict convexity identifies its supplied feasible minimizer with the canonical choice. Induction gives the same Option run. Apply the corresponding general source bound and substitute the quadratic geometry, preserving the signed movement term. This description separates the intended mathematical route from the limited exported constant-occurrence evidence.\",\n+            \"lean_notes\": \"Receive the entire current loss before choosing the new point and pay that loss at the new point. Lean loss t and eta t are source round t+1: center x(t), output/paid point x(t+1). This differs from ordinary OGD, which scores loss t at x(t). The conclusion identifies the SAME partial Option iterate at every prefix; it is conditional on attained updates and does not assert universal existence. The ambient assumptions above belong to the theorem; the full-proof source link exposes its section context. Selected actual compiled VALUE occurrences: hasStrictFDerivAt_norm_sq, HasGradientAt.fderiv_apply, norm_sub_sq_real. Occurrence is not necessity or a complete transitive graph. Locally compiled candidate; independent production BODY, complete canary BODY, combined project and final package acceptance pending. All seven Chapter2 forward containers and six future claims remain open; Chapter2 partial, accepted=false, proof denominator=null and Chapters1–16 GoalACTIVE. No source-container closure, main or live-publication claim.\",\n+            \"dependencies\": [\n+              \"hasStrictFDerivAt_norm_sq\",\n+              \"HasGradientAt.fderiv_apply\",\n+              \"norm_sub_sq_real\"\n+            ]\n+          }\n+        },\n+        {\n+          \"op\": \"add\",\n+          \"path\": \"/highlights/-\",\n+          \"value\": {\n+            \"full_name\": \"BanditRL.OnlinePrescientBregman.euclidean_variable_regret\",\n+            \"title\": \"Prescient Euclidean bound with decreasing steps\",\n+            \"chapter\": \"online-ogd\",\n+            \"featured\": false,\n+            \"teaching_order\": 331,\n+            \"source_match\": \"closest-source\",\n+            \"plain\": \"Finite-dimensional real inner-product E with NormedAddCommGroup E, InnerProductSpace ℝ E and FiniteDimensional ℝ E. V is closed, nonempty and convex. Played EReal losses have no bottom anywhere, are finite on V, and have ambient global supports at every point of V. Each supplied x(t+1) actually attains the squared-distance-penalized minimum on V; initialization x(0)=x0 is fixed. x0 need not belong to V. There is no affine, smooth-loss, globally finite-loss, bounded-gradient or bounded-domain restriction. T>0; positive nonincreasing used steps. Previous-state maximum excludes x(T).\",\n+            \"math\": \"R_T(u)\\\\le\\\\frac{\\\\max_{0\\\\le s<T}\\\\frac12\\\\|u-x_s\\\\|^2}{\\\\eta_{T-1}}-\\\\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\\\\frac{\\\\|x_{t+1}-x_t\\\\|^2}{2\\\\eta_t}.\",\n+            \"intuition\": \"Current-loss access changes the paid point. Movement contributes negatively, while the comparator potential remains.\",\n+            \"why\": \"One of three declaration-bound parts of the same prescient Euclidean lesson.\",\n+            \"position\": \"Algorithm15.8/Theorem15.30, PDF277–278; C2 pointer PDF26. Quadratic X=univ specialization; fixed proof exercise remains mandatory. The author’s constrained optimality/global-support step on PDF277 retains an unresolved source-proof justification. The alternative proximal-comparison route does not certify or erase that claim.\",\n+            \"proof_idea\": \"The quadratic derivative gives half squared distance as the shared divergence. Rewrite each actual penalized objective; strict convexity identifies its supplied feasible minimizer with the canonical choice. Induction gives the same Option run. Apply the corresponding general source bound and substitute the quadratic geometry, preserving the signed movement term. This description separates the intended mathematical route from the limited exported constant-occurrence evidence.\",\n+            \"lean_notes\": \"Receive the entire current loss before choosing the new point and pay that loss at the new point. Lean loss t and eta t are source round t+1: center x(t), output/paid point x(t+1). This differs from ordinary OGD, which scores loss t at x(t). The conclusion identifies the SAME partial Option iterate at every prefix; it is conditional on attained updates and does not assert universal existence. The ambient assumptions above belong to the theorem; the full-proof source link exposes its section context. Selected actual compiled VALUE occurrences: BanditRL.OnlineBregman.quadratic_geometry, BanditRL.OnlineConvex.sourceProper_of_domain, BanditRL.OnlinePrescientBregman.iterate_eq_of_source_updates, BanditRL.OnlinePrescientBregman.source_variable_regret. Occurrence is not necessity or a complete transitive graph. Locally compiled candidate; independent production BODY, complete canary BODY, combined project and final package acceptance pending. All seven Chapter2 forward containers and six future claims remain open; Chapter2 partial, accepted=false, proof denominator=null and Chapters1–16 GoalACTIVE. No source-container closure, main or live-publication claim.\",\n+            \"dependencies\": [\n+              \"BanditRL.OnlineBregman.quadratic_geometry\",\n+              \"BanditRL.OnlineConvex.sourceProper_of_domain\",\n+              \"BanditRL.OnlinePrescientBregman.iterate_eq_of_source_updates\",\n+              \"BanditRL.OnlinePrescientBregman.source_variable_regret\"\n+            ]\n+          }\n+        },\n+        {\n+          \"op\": \"add\",\n+          \"path\": \"/highlights/-\",\n+          \"value\": {\n+            \"full_name\": \"BanditRL.OnlinePrescientBregman.euclidean_fixed_regret\",\n+            \"title\": \"Prescient Euclidean bound with a fixed step\",\n+            \"chapter\": \"online-ogd\",\n+            \"featured\": false,\n+            \"teaching_order\": 332,\n+            \"source_match\": \"closest-source\",\n+            \"plain\": \"Finite-dimensional real inner-product E with NormedAddCommGroup E, InnerProductSpace ℝ E and FiniteDimensional ℝ E. V is closed, nonempty and convex. Played EReal losses have no bottom anywhere, are finite on V, and have ambient global supports at every point of V. Each supplied x(t+1) actually attains the squared-distance-penalized minimum on V; initialization x(0)=x0 is fixed. x0 need not belong to V. There is no affine, smooth-loss, globally finite-loss, bounded-gradient or bounded-domain restriction. eta>0; T=0 allowed, giving0<=||u-x0||²/(2eta). No empty maximum is needed.\",\n+            \"math\": \"R_T(u)\\\\le\\\\frac{\\\\|u-x_0\\\\|^2}{2\\\\eta}-\\\\frac1{2\\\\eta}\\\\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\\\\|x_{t+1}-x_t\\\\|^2.\",\n+            \"intuition\": \"Current-loss access changes the paid point. Movement contributes negatively, while the comparator potential remains.\",\n+            \"why\": \"One of three declaration-bound parts of the same prescient Euclidean lesson.\",\n+            \"position\": \"Algorithm15.8/Theorem15.30, PDF277–278; C2 pointer PDF26. Quadratic X=univ specialization; fixed proof exercise remains mandatory. The author’s constrained optimality/global-support step on PDF277 retains an unresolved source-proof justification. The alternative proximal-comparison route does not certify or erase that claim.\",\n+            \"proof_idea\": \"The quadratic derivative gives half squared distance as the shared divergence. Rewrite each actual penalized objective; strict convexity identifies its supplied feasible minimizer with the canonical choice. Induction gives the same Option run. Apply the corresponding general source bound and substitute the quadratic geometry, preserving the signed movement term. This description separates the intended mathematical route from the limited exported constant-occurrence evidence.\",\n+            \"lean_notes\": \"Receive the entire current loss before choosing the new point and pay that loss at the new point. Lean loss t and eta t are source round t+1: center x(t), output/paid point x(t+1). This differs from ordinary OGD, which scores loss t at x(t). The conclusion identifies the SAME partial Option iterate at every prefix; it is conditional on attained updates and does not assert universal existence. The ambient assumptions above belong to the theorem; the full-proof source link exposes its section context. Selected actual compiled VALUE occurrences: BanditRL.OnlineBregman.quadratic_geometry, BanditRL.OnlineConvex.sourceProper_of_domain, BanditRL.OnlinePrescientBregman.iterate_eq_of_source_updates, BanditRL.OnlinePrescientBregman.source_fixed_regret. Occurrence is not necessity or a complete transitive graph. Locally compiled candidate; independent production BODY, complete canary BODY, combined project and final package acceptance pending. All seven Chapter2 forward containers and six future claims remain open; Chapter2 partial, accepted=false, proof denominator=null and Chapters1–16 GoalACTIVE. No source-container closure, main or live-publication claim.\",\n+            \"dependencies\": [\n+              \"BanditRL.OnlineBregman.quadratic_geometry\",\n+              \"BanditRL.OnlineConvex.sourceProper_of_domain\",\n+              \"BanditRL.OnlinePrescientBregman.iterate_eq_of_source_updates\",\n+              \"BanditRL.OnlinePrescientBregman.source_fixed_regret\"\n+            ]\n+          }\n+        }\n+      ]\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \"root_import_proposals\": [\n+    {\n+      \"file\": \"BanditRLProof.lean\",\n+      \"append\": \"import BanditRLProof.OnlinePrescientEuclidean\",\n+      \"condition\": \"after independent production BODY and integration approval\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"file\": \"Tests.lean\",\n+      \"append\": \"import Tests.OnlinePrescientEuclideanCanary\",\n+      \"condition\": \"eventual only; confirm exact Test filename and accepted complete canary source before apply\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \"atomic_binder_audit\": [\n+    {\n+      \"declaration\": \"BanditRL.OnlineBregman.quadratic_geometry\",\n+      \"ambient\": [\n+        \"E : Type*\",\n+        \"NormedAddCommGroup E\",\n+        \"InnerProductSpace ℝ E\",\n+        \"CompleteSpace E\"\n+      ],\n+      \"inputs\": [\n+        \"x,y arbitrary\"\n+      ],\n+      \"conclusion_atoms\": [\n+        \"actual HasGradientAt psi y y\",\n+        \"Bpsi(x;y)=||x-y||²/2\"\n+      ]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"declaration\": \"BanditRL.OnlinePrescientBregman.euclidean_variable_regret\",\n+      \"ambient\": [\n+        \"E : Type*\",\n+        \"NormedAddCommGroup E\",\n+        \"InnerProductSpace ℝ E\",\n+        \"FiniteDimensional ℝ E\"\n+      ],\n+      \"inputs\": [\n+        \"convex/nonempty/closed V\",\n+        \"positive used eta\",\n+        \"T>0\",\n+        \"hinit\",\n+        \"played-pair nonincrease\",\n+        \"played global no-bottom\",\n+        \"finite on V\",\n+        \"global support at every feasible point\",\n+        \"actual feasible attained updates\",\n+        \"u in V\"\n+      ],\n+      \"conclusion_atoms\